.TH DIPISDS 1 "2026-08-17" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipisds \- announce or discover DVB-IPI services via DVBSTP/SD&S
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipisds
.B \-a
.B \-i
.I path
.B \-m
.IR mcast : port
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B dipisds
.B \-l
.B \-m
.IR mcast : port
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipisds
implements DVBSTP-carried SD&S service discovery per ETSI TS 102 034 clause 5.
It runs in one of two mutually exclusive modes, selected by
.B \-a
(announce, headend/injector role) or
.B \-l
(listen, client/receiver role); exactly one of the two is required.
.PP
In announce mode
.B dipisds
reads a service list from
.B \-i
and repeatedly transmits it as SD&S records over DVBSTP on the multicast
group:port given by
.BR \-m ,
at the interval set by
.B \-t
(default 5 seconds; ETSI TS 102 034 caps the full announce cycle at 30
seconds, so keep the interval comfortably under that). The input format is
inferred from the
.B \-i
suffix:
.B .csv
and
.B .m3u
use the same shapes as
.BR dipiscan (1)'s
own output,
.B .xspf
is XSPF with the DVB triplet carried in a dvbipitools extension element,
and
.B .xml
is a hand-authored or dipiscan-generated raw SD&S document that is sent
through unparsed. For the structured (non-.xml) inputs,
.B \-p
and
.B \-O
set the announced DomainName and provider display name, and
.B dipisds
additionally synthesizes a Service Provider Discovery record pointing back
at the same multicast socket. A set of
.BR \-\-ret\- ,
.BR \-\-fcc\- ,
.BR \-\-packages ,
.BR \-\-cells ,
.BR \-\-rms\- ,
and
.B \-\-fus\-
options extend the announced Broadcast Discovery and RMS-FUS records for
dipifccret RET/FCC retransmission servers, Package Discovery, Regionalisation
Discovery, and RMS-FUS Discovery. These options are announce-only and, with
the exception of the metrics options, have no effect on raw
.B .xml
input, which bypasses this processing entirely. SIGHUP re-reads
.B \-i
without restarting the process.
.PP
In listen mode
.B dipisds
joins the multicast group given by
.BR \-m ,
reassembles DVBSTP segments, and after
.B \-t
seconds (default 35, just over the spec's 30-second max cycle time so one
full announce cycle is always captured) writes whatever Broadcast Discovery
records it saw as a playlist to
.B \-o
(default stdout). The output format is selected by
.B \-f
or inferred from the
.B \-o
suffix:
.BR m3u ,
.BR csv ,
and
.B xspf
mirror
.BR dipiscan (1)'s
own shapes;
.B xml
dumps the reassembled SD&S document as received, for debugging; and
.B null
discards the output.
.PP
.B \-I
selects the network interface used for the multicast join or send,
overriding the kernel's default multicast route.
.B \-v
prints periodic statistics to stderr: one line per announce cycle in
.BR \-a ,
one line per segment received in
.BR \-l .
.B \-d
forks to the background and detaches from the controlling terminal after
startup.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Mode selection
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-announce
Headend mode: read
.BR \-i ,
transmit on
.BR \-m .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-listen
Client mode: receive on
.BR \-m ,
write
.BR \-o .
.SS Common options
.TP
.BI \-m " group" : port
.RB ( \-\-mcast )
Multicast group:port. Use
.RI [ addr6 ]: port
for IPv6. Required in both modes.
.TP
.BI \-I " iface"
.RB ( \-\-iface )
Multicast interface.
.TP
.BI \-t " seconds"
Announce mode
.RB ( \-\-interval ):
repeat interval, default 5. Listen mode
.RB ( \-\-timeout ):
stop after N seconds, default 35.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Periodic stats on stderr.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " when"
.RI ( auto | always | never ,
default
.BR auto ).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SS Announce mode options (\-a)
.TP
.BI \-i " path"
.RB ( \-\-input )
A
.BR .csv / .m3u / .xspf
playlist or raw SD&S
.B .xml
document.
.TP
.BI \-p " name"
.RB ( \-\-provider )
DomainName. Required unless
.B \-i
is
.BR .xml .
.TP
.BI \-O " name"
.RB ( \-\-offering )
Display name. Required unless
.B \-i
is
.BR .xml .
.TP
.BI \-L " code"
.RB ( \-\-lang )
ISO 639-2 code for the display name (default
.BR deu ).
.TP
.BI \-\-ret\-addr " addr" : port
Advertise a
.BR dipifccret (1)
RET server (its
.B \-l
value). Opt-in; adds RTPRetransmission to every announced service.
.TP
.BI \-\-ret\-rtx\-time " ms"
RET rtx-time, matches
.BR dipifccret (1)'s
.B \-B
(default 2000).
.TP
.BI \-\-ret\-rtx\-pt " n"
RET RTP payload type, matches
.BR dipifccret (1)'s
.B \-R
(default 99).
.TP
.B \-\-ret\-mc
Also advertise multicast RET (as
.BR dipifccret (1)
does without
.BR \-\-no\-mc\-ret ).
.TP
.BI \-\-ret\-mc\-port " port"
Multicast RET port, matches
.BR dipifccret (1)'s
.BR \-F .
Default: each service's own port.
.TP
.B \-\-ret\-rsi\-mc\-ret
RSI (Annex F.5.3) rides the multicast RET session instead of the default
session. Requires
.BR \-\-ret\-mc ;
matches
.BR dipifccret (1)'s
.BR \-\-rsi\-mc\-ret .
.TP
.BI \-\-fcc\-addr " addr" : port
Advertise a
.BR dipifccret (1)
FCC server (its
.B \-l
value). Opt-in; adds ServerBasedEnhancementServiceInfo to every announced
service.
.TP
.BI \-\-fcc\-rtx\-time " ms"
FCC Retransmission_session rtx-time (default 2000).
.TP
.BI \-\-fcc\-rtx\-pt " n"
FCC RTP payload type, matches
.BR dipifccret (1)'s
.B \-R
(default 99).
.TP
.B \-\-fcc\-resolve\-by\-port
Per-service FCC port instead of
.BR \-\-fcc\-addr 's
port. Matches
.BR dipifccret (1)'s
.BR \-\-fcc\-resolve\-by\-port .
.TP
.BI \-\-fcc\-resolve\-base\-port " port"
Matches
.BR dipifccret (1)'s
.BR \-\-fcc\-resolve\-base\-port .
.TP
.BI \-\-fcc\-resolve\-max\-channels " n"
Must match
.BR dipifccret (1)'s
.B \-M
(default 384).
.TP
.BI \-\-metrics " path"
Unix datagram socket for metrics (default
.IR /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock ).
.TP
.BI \-\-metrics\-id " name"
Stable instance id. Metrics are disabled unless this is set.
.TP
.BI \-\-metrics\-interval " seconds"
Snapshot interval (default 5).
.TP
.BI \-\-packages " path"
Package Discovery from
.I id,name,lang,visible,svc1|svc2|...
lines.
.TP
.BI \-\-cells " path"
Regionalisation Discovery from
.I id,country,type:value,...
lines.
.TP
.BI \-\-rms\-name " name"
RMS Discovery display name. Requires
.BR \-\-rms\-location .
.TP
.BI \-\-rms\-lang " code"
ISO 639-2 code for
.B \-\-rms\-name
(default
.BR deu ).
.TP
.BI \-\-rms\-location " uri"
RMSType RMSLocation.
.TP
.BI \-\-rms\-logo " uri"
RMSType LogoURI.
.TP
.BI \-\-fus\-name " name"
FUS Discovery display name. Requires
.BR \-\-fus\-id .
.TP
.BI \-\-fus\-lang " code"
ISO 639-2 code for
.B \-\-fus\-name
(default
.BR deu ).
.TP
.BI \-\-fus\-id " n"
FUSID (decimal).
.TP
.BI \-\-fus\-announce " addr" : port
FUS MulticastAnnouncementAddress.
.TP
.BI \-\-fus\-logo " uri"
FUSType LogoURI.
.SS Listen mode options (\-l)
.TP
.BI \-o " path"
.RB ( \-\-output )
Output path,
.B \-
for stdout (default).
.TP
.BI \-f " fmt"
.RB ( \-\-format )
.RI ( m3u | csv | xspf | xml | null ,
default taken from the
.B \-o
suffix).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipisds \-a \-i channels.csv \-p example.org \-O "My Headend" \-m 239.255.0.1:3937
Announce a CSV playlist as an SD&S service list.
.TP
.B dipisds \-l \-m 239.255.0.1:3937 \-o discovered.m3u
Listen for the announcement and write the discovered services as an m3u playlist.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B non-zero
Argument error, or I/O or network failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipiscan (1),
.BR dipibcg (1),
.BR dipifccret (1)
.PP
